Night mode: the Phone LED can be put out too

The phone LED (green:phone) belongs to the phone service (awvoice-phoned), which restores the
lamp whenever another program writes it, so night mode had no Phone entry and left the lamp lit
all night. With patches/packages/awvoice-phoned/0001 the phone service takes a memory-only hold
over ubus (`awvoice indicator_dark`), and this asks for it:

- the daemon (phone_update, run with night_update on every tick) holds the lamp dark while the
  night window is open and 'phone' is not in the exempt list, releases it when the window closes,
  sends the hold again about once a minute (the phone service forgets it when it restarts), and
  releases it when the daemon stops or `cw-led-daemon restore` runs. Without the phone service the
  call fails quietly and is tried again a minute later. The first tick after a start sends the
  current state either way, which also clears a hold a crashed daemon left behind.
- the settings page offers Phone in "Keep on during night", and says the lamp belongs to the phone
  service.
- the shipped config exempts 'phone' like every other LED, so night mode changes nothing until the
  user unticks it; 90-cw-led adds 'phone' once to a config written before this, so an upgrade does
  not put the lamp out unasked (cw-led.night.phone_known marks it done).

